Why: design 10 P4, the sixth framing rule: "A printed line that begins with end-marker text is plain text too unless
a message of that code is open at that moment". Line 7 begins with the 2185 end marker and has text after it, with no
message open: one plain line. Line 10 is the same while a 2201 is open: a body line of that 2201. No capture shows
this (research 1's print-marker has the marker text inside quotes).

How: Written by hand (TLC did not produce this shape; research 1 tried). The messages around it are copied from tlc/v1.7.4/success.out: 2262 (version), 2185 (start) and 2186 (finish). Lines 7 and 10 are new; the 2201 text is taken from tlc/v1.7.4/coverage.out.
